From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cennac <cennac@163.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: clamp AP6275P APCF vendor capability

The AP6275P vendor capability response advertises APCF support with 16
filters, but the controller does not implement the Android LE_ADV_FILTER
vendor command correctly. The GD scanning manager override does not cover the
legacy BTM advertising filter implementation, which consumes the same raw
capability response and continues to send opcode 0xfd57.

Clamp the legacy capability at its source so BTIF, Java feature reporting,
BTM initialization, and every BTM APCF entry point consistently use the
existing unsupported path. Ordinary controller-based LE scanning is not
affected.
---
 system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc b/system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc
index 04f6994f87..0000000000 100644
--- a/system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc
+++ b/system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc
@@ -699,0 +700,8 @@
+  // AP6275P reports APCF support but rejects Android vendor opcode 0xfd57.
+  // Clamp the capability before BTIF or legacy BTM can initialize offload.
+  if (btm_cb.cmn_ble_vsc_cb.filter_support != 0 ||
+      btm_cb.cmn_ble_vsc_cb.max_filter != 0) {
+    LOG(WARNING) << "AGIBOT AP6275P: disabling unsupported APCF offload";
+  }
+  btm_cb.cmn_ble_vsc_cb.filter_support = 0;
+  btm_cb.cmn_ble_vsc_cb.max_filter = 0;
+
-- 
